  "_note": "A made-up report of add-in 0.13.0 (report version 2, fields added) of the new-model job (flo2-rvt 0.14.0, change-list version 5), shaped as flo2's own fixtures of a list and its report, for change_list: a model made from Revit's own no-template project in imperial units (new_model), two new levels (add_level), four walls on the lower rising to the upper, a floor and a room inside them, and a wall of a type the new model does not hold (not applied, naming the one it holds). What Revit's own no-template project holds (its starting levels, levels_at_start, and its types) is made up here; a new model's file section is the saved model.rvt's, as Revit reads its header: it is unproven until the first real run, whose report lists them (types). Points are in feet, in internal coordinates, which in a new model are its shared ones (coordinates: no turn, no offset). The walls are 8 in thick on their centre lines, so the room is bounded at their faces, 39 ft 4 in by 24 ft 4 in. Read by server/test/new-model.test.ts and addin/tests, and copied unchanged into flo2 (services/edge-gateway/test/fixtures/rvt-new-model-report.json) for its check.",
